%% hNFT Gate 0.2, ADR-0001 — proposed protocol, NOT approved.
%% Canonical ownership changes ONLY when the seller authors Finalization.
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> Owned: mint or prior finalized state
    Owned --> Offered: owner authors Offer
    Offered --> Accepted: named buyer authors Acceptance
(provisional, no title)
    Accepted --> Finalized: owner authors valid Finalization
(only title-changing transition)
    Finalized --> Owned: new owner state = Finalization action
    Offered --> Cancelled: owner authors Cancellation
(<= accept_by)
    Accepted --> Cancelled: valid Acceptance orphaned
if seller cancels before Finalization
    Offered --> Expired: owner authors Expiry
(> finalize_by)
    Accepted --> Expired: Acceptance orphaned
if no Finalization by cutoff
    Cancelled --> Owned: original owner retained
    Expired --> Owned: original owner retained

    note right of Offered
        Only one active Offer for each owner state.
        No DHT link or signal authorizes title.
    end note
    note right of Accepted
        Remote acceptance and seller close can race.
        Accepted is an observed workflow stage,
        never an authoritative ownership state.
    end note
    note right of Finalized
        Finalization and Cancellation/Expiry are
        exclusive seller-chain terminal events.
        Finalization consumes prev_owner_state.
    end note
